{"id":"NCT06380192","title":"Developmental and Epileptic Encephalopathy of Genetic Etiology: Natural History Through Reuse of Clinical Data","official":"Developmental and Epileptic Encephalopathy of Genetic Etiology: Natural History Through Reuse of Clinical Data / DEE-RETRO","summary":"Developmental and Epileptic Encephalopathy (DEE) are a heterogeneous group of neurodevelopmental disorders linked to both epilepsy and its underlying etiology, independently of epileptiform activity.\n\nThe creation of a database with retrospective follow-up of a large number of patients on a national scale will enable better knowledge of specific biomarkers, and thus a better classification and understanding of the natural evolution of DEE according to their etiology. This will enable better, more personalized therapeutic management of patients, depending on etiology and the presence or absence of these biomarkers. The investigators will also be able to draw up management recommendations, which are currently non-existent.","conditions":["Developmental and Epileptic Encephalopathy"],"interventions":[],"criteria":"Inclusion Criteria:\n\n* Diagnosis of Developmental and Epileptic Encephalopathy\n* Registered with or benefiting from a social security scheme.\n\nExclusion Criteria:\n\n* Opposition of the patient or his/her parents to the re-use of data in the context of this study\n* Person subject to a safeguard of justice measure","minAge":"","maxAge":"","sex":"ALL","healthy":false,"studyType":"OBSERVATIONAL","purpose":"","enrollment":400,"start":"2024-10-31","pcd":"2026-12-31","upd":"2025-06-29","sponsor":"Imagine Institute","areas":["neurology"],"central":["Rima Nabbout, Pr · +33144381536 · rima.nabbout@aphp.fr"],"sites":[{"f":"CHU Amiens","city":"Amiens","pr":"","zip":"","s":"NYR","lat":49.9,"lon":2.3,"c":"William Szurhaj, Pr · Szurhaj.William@chu-amiens.fr"},{"f":"CH Angers","city":"Angers","pr":"","zip":"","s":"NYR","lat":47.4716,"lon":-0.552,"c":"Patrick Van Bogaert, Pr · Patrick